# ==============================================================================
# Generated data — all reproducible via tar_make()
# ==============================================================================
analysis/data/derived_data/
*.npy
*.npz
*.rds

# ==============================================================================
# targets cache — reproducible via tar_make()
# ==============================================================================
_targets/
analysis/paper/_targets/
analysis/robustness/_targets_store/
# Quarto/SI render log (generated artifact)
analysis/robustness/_si_render.log
# Robustness sensitivity — regenerated outputs (recomputed by the SI tar_make).
# The required INPUTS (spectra/ and scar_attrition*.csv) are intentionally NOT
# ignored.
#
# The figures are ignored as CONTENTS (`figures/*`), not as a directory: a
# trailing-slash rule would exclude the directory itself, and git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so the two `!` exceptions below could
# never take effect. Those two are inputs, not regenerated outputs — nothing in
# CI redraws them, so ignoring them broke the reproducibility workflow:
#   * fig_S_perturbation_combined.png — the `perturbation_figure_png` file
#     target in _targets_supplementary.R (the sweep that produces it is run
#     offline, so the pipeline consumes the committed PNG), and supplementary.qmd
#   * fig_joint_mfa_main.png — included by manuscript.qmd (@fig-exp-joint-mfa)
analysis/robustness/*/figures/*
!analysis/robustness/annotation_perturbation/figures/fig_S_perturbation_combined.png
!analysis/robustness/joint_mfa_discrimination/figures/fig_joint_mfa_main.png
analysis/robustness/*/sweep_manifest.csv
analysis/robustness/*/*_metrics.csv
analysis/robustness/*/*_orderselection_by_degree.csv
analysis/robustness/*/*_curves.csv
analysis/robustness/mesh_decimation_sensitivity/determinism_*.csv
analysis/robustness/scar_threshold_sensitivity/im_threshold_diagnostic.csv

# ==============================================================================
# Analysis output (figures, HTML, rendered docs)
# ==============================================================================
analysis/output/
*.html
*.docx
*.pdf
figure origin/
# keep the Word reference template (formatting, not a rendered output)
!analysis/templates/template.docx
!analysis/paper/manuscript.docx
!analysis/paper/manuscript.pdf

